ThehasNextByte()method returnstrueif the next token represents a number that can be stored by thebytedata type, which is any whole number between -128 and 127.

If theradixparameter is used, then it interprets numbers using the radix. For example, a radix of 16 would interpret numbers as hexadecimal (digits 0 to 9 and A to F). If theradixparameter is not used then it interprets numbers using the scanner's radix, which is 10 by default but it can be changed with theuseRadix()method.

